    {
      "text": "The initial CoCrFeMnNi alloy is in a solidified, single-phase solid-solution state.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512474::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Eliminating Co from equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi produces the quaternary FeNiCrMn alloy used for comparison.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed comparison spans approximately 300–700 K and strain rates from 10^-3 to 10^3 s^-1.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512474::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removing Co from CoCrFeMnNi raises the effective stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9448438::web::006::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co removal modifies the dislocation-core structure and may shift local chemical order.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher stacking-fault energy lowers the barrier for dislocation cross-slip in the Co-free alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher stacking-fault energy accelerates dynamic recovery in the Co-free alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced cross-slip and recovery reduce dislocation accumulation and local stress concentrations under dynamic loading.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced dislocation accumulation produces more uniform plastic flow.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi, FeNiCrMn will have lower strain-rate sensitivity.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi, FeNiCrMn will show a less pronounced decline in yield stress as temperature increases.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "FeNiCrMn will show more evidence of dislocation cross-slip and dynamic recovery than CoCrFeMnNi under matched conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism preserves a favorable strength–ductility balance in FeNiCrMn across the stated temperature and strain-rate range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stacking-fault-energy-mediated mechanism is predicted to dominate from 300 to 700 K and from quasi-static rates to roughly 10^3 s^-1.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At cryogenic temperatures, twinning may supersede the proposed cross-slip and recovery mechanism.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9448438::web::006::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At extreme high temperatures, diffusion-dominated recovery may supersede the proposed mechanism.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
